{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on whether a lottery has a sure outcome (i.e., an outcome with 100% probability). In this decision problem, Lottery A offers 5 Euros with 100% probability, which is a sure outcome. Lottery B offers 5000 Euros with 0.1% probability and 0 Euros with 99.9% probability—neither outcome is certain. Therefore, Lottery A has a sure outcome, and Lottery B does not. The decision reason prefers the lottery *without* a sure outcome, which would be Lottery B. Thus, the reason can be applied: it would lead to a preference for B over A.",
